# 6. CUSTOMER-FUNDED BUSINESS MODEL

THIS IS A CRITICAL BUSINESS REQUIREMENT.

The application owner must not be required to personally purchase AI API credits, image-generation credits, hosting upgrades or other paid services as an automatic operating requirement.

The business model must use customer subscription and usage revenue to fund operating costs.

### Financial principles

1. Customers pay for the plans and services they use.
2. Customer revenue funds AI generation, hosting, storage, email and payment-processing costs.
3. DEDSEC monitors usage and operating expenses.
4. Subscription prices must be configurable.
5. Generation quotas must be configurable.
6. The application must protect against uncontrolled provider usage.
7. No paid service may be activated automatically without explicit approval.
8. No hidden charges or unexpected spending.

### Important operating limitation

External AI providers, hosting companies and email services may require prepaid balances, minimum charges or paid accounts.

Do not claim that the application can operate completely free if the selected provider requires payment.

If a provider requires upfront payment, explain that requirement and offer a genuinely usable free or open-source alternative where available.

Never purchase credits or upgrade services automatically.

### Free plan

The preferred initial Free plan target is 300 image generations per month.

However, the Free plan must only be enabled at that quota when its operating cost is covered by genuinely free provider capacity, local infrastructure, sponsorship or an explicitly approved business budget.

Otherwise, make the Free quota configurable or offer a limited free trial.

Never silently subsidise free usage using the owner's personal money.

